    "notes": "Polyethylene Terephthalate Glycol (PETG) printed via FDM. Glycol modification prevents the brittleness of standard PET. Good balance of strength, toughness, chemical resistance, and printability — often considered the best all-around FDM material. Water and chemically resistant per Simplify3D. Fatigue resistant. Higher service temperature than PLA. Properties are anisotropic; use XY-oriented load paths for structural parts."
